00:08:35.775 --> 00:08:36.608
- Oh, thank you.

00:08:36.608 --> 00:08:37.441
- [H] All right.

00:08:37.441 --> 00:08:40.358
- Gently slide it in away from you.

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:42.503
(triumphant music)

00:08:42.503 --> 00:08:43.336
Yeah!

00:08:43.336 --> 00:08:44.616
(H claps)

00:08:44.616 --> 00:08:45.665
- If I lose because of the cake...

00:08:45.665 --> 00:08:46.498
(Owen laughs)

00:08:46.498 --> 00:08:47.331
I swear to God.

00:08:47.331 --> 00:08:48.786
My California roll mixer is done

00:08:48.786 --> 00:08:50.536
and I'm gonna start seasoning my rice.

00:08:50.536 --> 00:08:51.369
(rice plops against glass and wood)

00:08:51.369 --> 00:08:52.657
- Dude!
(H laughs)

00:08:52.657 --> 00:08:54.573
- Rice vinegar, salt, sugar.

00:08:54.573 --> 00:08:57.639
- I will say, this worries
me seeing him make rice.

00:08:57.639 --> 00:09:01.041
Because, to be honest, the
best sushi rice I've ever had

00:09:01.041 --> 00:09:02.384
is from H.

00:09:02.384 --> 00:09:04.590
- Making sure every grain is coated.

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:07.671
It's a little too seasoned, but...

00:09:07.671 --> 00:09:08.505
It's like too seasoned.

00:09:08.505 --> 00:09:10.413
It's too much vinegar.

00:09:10.413 --> 00:09:11.965
- That was not the rice
I was talking about.

00:09:11.965 --> 00:09:12.823
- No. (chuckles)

00:09:12.823 --> 00:09:14.231
I'm just not in my element.

00:09:14.231 --> 00:09:16.776
This is like not my rice cooker, nor-

00:09:16.776 --> 00:09:17.609
- Huh.

00:09:17.609 --> 00:09:18.650
- the right amount I use.

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:20.990
Can I please borrow some of your rice?

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:22.993
- So you want to take some of my rice?

00:09:22.993 --> 00:09:23.970
- Mhmm.

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:26.991
- I was a little taken aback
when H asked to use my rice

00:09:26.991 --> 00:09:30.581
to make his rice better, but
since he lended me a hand

00:09:30.581 --> 00:09:32.628
in getting the rice in the fryer,

00:09:32.628 --> 00:09:33.973
I'm obviously gonna help him out.

00:09:33.973 --> 00:09:34.867
Yeah. You got it.

00:09:34.867 --> 00:09:35.874
- Okay, thank you. (laughs)

00:09:35.874 --> 00:09:36.707
This is looking great.

00:09:36.707 --> 00:09:39.608
We got that nice golden
crust on the outside.

00:09:39.608 --> 00:09:40.710
So we're just gonna transfer it over

00:09:40.710 --> 00:09:42.626
and let it drain and cool.

00:09:42.626 --> 00:09:47.282
- So now we're gonna form our
yellow sushi ball berry thing.

00:09:47.282 --> 00:09:50.642
To make it yellow, we're gonna
use yuzu or yellow tobiko.

00:09:50.642 --> 00:09:53.404
So our base layer, you gotta
be very gentle with this stuff.

00:09:53.404 --> 00:09:57.054
- I think H is taking a big
risk with the sushi balls.

00:09:57.054 --> 00:09:59.148
He's covering it in fish eggs.

00:09:59.148 --> 00:10:01.880
I don't know what nine
year old likes that.

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:04.446
- Next layer is rice.

00:10:04.446 --> 00:10:06.063
A little bit of our filling,

00:10:06.063 --> 00:10:07.803
a little bit more rice to seal that.

00:10:07.803 --> 00:10:10.062
So you pull this all together,

00:10:10.062 --> 00:10:12.544
and try to get all the air out,

00:10:12.544 --> 00:10:15.010
and you're gonna twist
and form a sushi ball.

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:16.492
Unravel this puppy.

00:10:16.492 --> 00:10:18.616
I'm gonna add little stems.

00:10:18.616 --> 00:10:19.866
- That ain't it. That ain't it.

00:10:19.866 --> 00:10:20.699
- It's cute!

00:10:20.699 --> 00:10:21.977
- That is not a yellow berry.

00:10:21.977 --> 00:10:23.672
- This is an interpretation. (laughs)

00:10:23.672 --> 00:10:25.386
I think it looks more like a yellow brain.

00:10:25.386 --> 00:10:26.774
Either way it doesn't look that great,

00:10:26.774 --> 00:10:28.128
but when you put the little stem on top,

00:10:28.128 --> 00:10:29.260
I think it looks cute.

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:31.684
- Now I'm gonna show you how
to make real yellow berries.

00:10:31.684 --> 00:10:34.243
So we're gonna start by
cleaning up the pineapple.

00:10:34.243 --> 00:10:35.582
So I have this ring mold

00:10:35.582 --> 00:10:38.350
that kind of resembles like a berry shape.

00:10:38.350 --> 00:10:41.119
Oh! Ha ha! That's pretty cool.

00:10:41.119 --> 00:10:43.744
So I am making punctures in the pineapple

00:10:43.744 --> 00:10:47.332
to put in the little airhead stems.

00:10:47.332 --> 00:10:49.625
- My chicken has frozen.

00:10:49.625 --> 00:10:51.508
Gonna punch 'em out
with these star shapes.

00:10:51.508 --> 00:10:54.441
Flour, egg wash, Ritz cracker breadcrumb.

00:10:54.441 --> 00:10:57.354
- All right, so now we
have our puff pastry stars.

00:10:57.354 --> 00:10:58.642
These are great. Look at that.

00:10:58.642 --> 00:10:59.872
Now we just gotta turn them red.

00:10:59.872 --> 00:11:02.314
And so to do that, we
have even more cheese.

00:11:02.314 --> 00:11:04.056
Mix that with some red food coloring,

00:11:04.056 --> 00:11:05.935
and then we're just
gonna coat it, toss it,

00:11:05.935 --> 00:11:07.474
and that's a red cheese star.

00:11:07.474 --> 00:11:08.307
Look at that.

00:11:08.307 --> 00:11:10.627
- That looks radioactive.

00:11:10.627 --> 00:11:13.367
Why does it look like a
nuclear power plant? (laughs)

00:11:13.367 --> 00:11:14.576
- He may think it's radioactive.

00:11:14.576 --> 00:11:18.038
I think Maxley will think it
looks identical to the picture.

00:11:18.038 --> 00:11:19.358
- Bang, fry.

00:11:19.358 --> 00:11:20.191
(hot oil sizzling)

00:11:20.191 --> 00:11:21.835
Dude, look at that.

00:11:21.835 --> 00:11:23.312
That looks unreal.

00:11:23.312 --> 00:11:24.145
- That's pretty cool.

00:11:24.145 --> 00:11:28.106
- My final stage, I'm gonna
dust this... ketchup powder.

00:11:28.106 --> 00:11:31.784
Bang! Red stars that aren't radioactive.

00:11:31.784 --> 00:11:33.628
- Dude, that looks just as gnarly as this.

00:11:33.628 --> 00:11:34.461
(H laughs)

00:11:34.461 --> 00:11:36.068
- My banana bread cake is done.

00:11:36.068 --> 00:11:37.719
So I'm just cutting off
the top to flatten it

00:11:37.719 --> 00:11:40.621
and create my three
tiered banana bread cake.

00:11:40.621 --> 00:11:42.697
- I'm gonna be shaving
off some vegetables.

00:11:42.697 --> 00:11:43.929
Got a bunch of different colors here.

00:11:43.929 --> 00:11:47.000
Yellow strips, purple cabbage, green...

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:49.507
We're gonna use his favorite vegetable:

00:11:49.507 --> 00:11:51.006
good old broccoli.

00:11:51.006 --> 00:11:52.422
- Look at that. That looks sick.

00:11:52.422 --> 00:11:53.430
- That's a cake.

00:11:53.430 --> 00:11:55.964
- I am not an expert at frosting.

00:11:55.964 --> 00:11:57.733
- Your mom is a great baker, though.

00:11:57.733 --> 00:11:58.860
- My mom is a great baker.

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.057
- [Producer] Do you know H's mom well?

00:12:00.057 --> 00:12:01.831
- I do know H's mom quite well.

00:12:01.831 --> 00:12:02.664
(H chuckles)

00:12:02.664 --> 00:12:04.383
She would... (laughs)

00:12:04.383 --> 00:12:06.800
(both laugh)

00:12:08.938 --> 00:12:10.005
Hi, Susan!

00:12:10.005 --> 00:12:11.216
- No, they get along well.

00:12:11.216 --> 00:12:12.094
(producer laughs)

00:12:12.094 --> 00:12:13.080
They get along really well.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:14.870
So we're gonna start off with
our ocean mist right now.

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:17.957
I have a bunch of
delicious ingredients here.

00:12:17.957 --> 00:12:19.247
All natural.

00:12:19.247 --> 00:12:20.198
What's that over there?

00:12:20.198 --> 00:12:22.665
- All right, hear me out.
Kids love all of this.

00:12:22.665 --> 00:12:23.498
(H laughs)

00:12:23.498 --> 00:12:27.340
We got ingredients for a
Mountain Dew Baja Blast.

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:29.315
And now to make this magical drink,

00:12:29.315 --> 00:12:32.305
add some honey around the rim,
roll it in some pop rocks,

00:12:32.305 --> 00:12:35.115
an even ratio of Mountain Dew and Sprite,

00:12:35.115 --> 00:12:38.994
and then the rest will
be Frost Cool Gatorade.

00:12:38.994 --> 00:12:41.936
And then this is blue and it's sugar,

00:12:41.936 --> 00:12:44.393
so I'm gonna put it in
inside the cup as well.

00:12:44.393 --> 00:12:47.393
There you have it! Blue misty drink.

00:12:48.686 --> 00:12:51.497
- So to make this ocean
mist misty and oceany

00:12:51.497 --> 00:12:52.651
I'm gonna spoon in a powder.

00:12:52.651 --> 00:12:55.286
- My man, with your plate,
he's eating chicken nuggets,

00:12:55.286 --> 00:12:57.552
a whole cake, sushi balls....

00:12:57.552 --> 00:12:59.594
He's gonna be quite parched.

00:12:59.594 --> 00:13:02.559
And does he want to, like,
take down a thick shake?

00:13:02.559 --> 00:13:03.392
No. He is gonna want

00:13:03.392 --> 00:13:07.153
some nice cool misty
Mountain Dew Baja Blast.

00:13:07.153 --> 00:13:07.986
- You know...

00:13:07.986 --> 00:13:08.819
- That's my thought process.

00:13:08.819 --> 00:13:10.049
- You do you.

00:13:10.049 --> 00:13:12.667
My thought process was
nailing each component.

00:13:12.667 --> 00:13:15.200
I don't think that a nine
year old is gonna think

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:17.423
about the balance of an
entire composed dish.

00:13:17.423 --> 00:13:19.022
- All right, drinks are done.

00:13:19.022 --> 00:13:22.036
Let's play it up and present it.

00:13:22.036 --> 00:13:22.869
- Yes, Chef.

00:13:22.869 --> 00:13:25.025
- My burger patties shrunk significantly,

00:13:25.025 --> 00:13:28.215
so I'm gonna have to basically
shrink everything else

00:13:28.215 --> 00:13:31.569
to make sure it has that
tier layer for the cake.

00:13:31.569 --> 00:13:32.573
- First thing I'm gonna deal with is

00:13:32.573 --> 00:13:34.356
decorating my banana bread cake.

00:13:34.356 --> 00:13:36.108
So I'm gonna first measure
some of these Twizzlers

00:13:36.108 --> 00:13:39.007
to line up the tier cake.

00:13:39.007 --> 00:13:40.934
Yours is a lot more difficult. (chuckles)

00:13:40.934 --> 00:13:43.907
- The gravy glue seems to be working nice.

00:13:43.907 --> 00:13:45.742
It's also gonna be very flavorful.

00:13:45.742 --> 00:13:49.110
And now I'm just gonna cut
a mold for the chicken.

00:13:49.110 --> 00:13:52.199
And the last part is just a fried egg.

00:13:52.199 --> 00:13:54.159
Look at that! That's a savory cake.

00:13:54.159 --> 00:13:56.346
- Do you think, when
Maxley tries your cake,

00:13:56.346 --> 00:13:57.887
he's gonna think Loco Moco?

00:13:57.887 --> 00:13:59.051
- I really hope so.

00:13:59.051 --> 00:13:59.925
(both laugh)

00:13:59.925 --> 00:14:03.121
- So now we're going
to decorate said cake.

00:14:03.121 --> 00:14:04.986
It's the cake for the Pokemon God.

00:14:04.986 --> 00:14:06.655
Realizing though that I need to decorate

00:14:06.655 --> 00:14:08.623
a bit more than I thought

00:14:08.623 --> 00:14:10.838
or else this cake looks pretty plain.

00:14:10.838 --> 00:14:11.671
- We'll add the red stars...

00:14:11.671 --> 00:14:15.451
So he has a few red stripes on there,

00:14:15.451 --> 00:14:19.484
I'm gonna just try to make
a few red lines with ketchup

00:14:19.484 --> 00:14:24.070
- Purely for spacing, I chose
this really big lazy Susan,

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:26.253
because this cake is what's-

00:14:26.253 --> 00:14:27.558
- What's a lazy Susan?

00:14:27.558 --> 00:14:29.092
- It's the term for
this. It's a lazy Susan.

00:14:29.092 --> 00:14:29.925
- What?!
- Yeah.

00:14:29.925 --> 00:14:30.758
- It's your mom's name.

00:14:30.758 --> 00:14:32.015
- It is my mom's name! (laughs)

00:14:32.015 --> 00:14:34.434
- My red stars on the plates.

00:14:34.434 --> 00:14:36.302
My yellow berries,

00:14:36.302 --> 00:14:39.415
and my wonderful ocean mist milkshake.

00:14:39.415 --> 00:14:40.582
And I am done.

00:14:41.537 --> 00:14:43.276
- All right, well let's
see what Maxley thinks.

00:14:43.276 --> 00:14:46.306
- And may the best cook win.

00:14:46.306 --> 00:14:48.227
("Brindisi" from La Traviata
by Giuseppe Verdi plays)

00:14:48.227 --> 00:14:52.280
Overall, I'm super happy with
the entire dish as a whole.

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:54.002
I'm really stoked with
how the cake turned out.

00:14:54.002 --> 00:14:56.472
I think you can clearly see each layer

00:14:56.472 --> 00:14:57.858
and the different colors.

00:14:57.858 --> 00:15:00.551
The red stars I think are identical.

00:15:00.551 --> 00:15:01.908
They also taste great.

00:15:01.908 --> 00:15:04.919
The blue drink I think is also super cool.

00:15:04.919 --> 00:15:06.335
Give him that mist effect.

00:15:06.335 --> 00:15:08.966
It's blue, it's sweet, it's sugar.

00:15:08.966 --> 00:15:10.173
What more do you want?

00:15:10.173 --> 00:15:12.442
The berries, it is just pineapple,

00:15:12.442 --> 00:15:15.228
but I added the green airheads.

00:15:15.228 --> 00:15:17.457
Hopefully he will be a fan of that.

00:15:17.457 --> 00:15:19.437
I think it looks a lot like the picture.

00:15:19.437 --> 00:15:20.880
I hope Maxley likes it too.

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:22.283
- I'm feeling pretty good about this dish.

00:15:22.283 --> 00:15:24.487
Starting with the cake,
I think it looks great.

00:15:24.487 --> 00:15:26.015
I think it looks like the picture,

00:15:26.015 --> 00:15:28.879
even though it's not a perfect
oval with a hundred colors.

00:15:28.879 --> 00:15:31.466
The yellow berries, I
think they look adorable,

00:15:31.466 --> 00:15:34.359
and they honestly look like
something out of Pokemon.

00:15:34.359 --> 00:15:35.580
He likes chicken cutlets;

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:38.604
I think chicken nuggets hit the spot.

00:15:38.604 --> 00:15:40.093
Ocean mist tastes great.

00:15:40.093 --> 00:15:41.472
I feel like every single kid in the world

00:15:41.472 --> 00:15:42.633
loves vanilla milkshakes.

00:15:42.633 --> 00:15:45.749
Hopefully Maxley enjoys
my plate more than Owen's,

00:15:45.749 --> 00:15:47.923
and I can take home the prize.

00:15:47.923 --> 00:15:50.150
- Bring on my dream Pokemon dish!

00:15:50.150 --> 00:15:52.608
(playful music)

00:15:52.608 --> 00:15:53.441
(cartoon flourish)

00:15:53.441 --> 00:15:54.358
Oh, my God!

00:15:55.395 --> 00:15:57.442
They actually went full out on this.

00:15:57.442 --> 00:16:00.181
It was actually supposed
to be green, not purple.

00:16:00.181 --> 00:16:02.770
- Maxley, I tried my best with the colors.

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:03.795
Just gimme a break.

00:16:03.795 --> 00:16:05.849
- And they actually did the umbrella.

00:16:05.849 --> 00:16:06.774
(Maxley claps)

00:16:06.774 --> 00:16:08.536
I think I'll eat the stars.

00:16:08.536 --> 00:16:09.587
That's chicken!

00:16:09.587 --> 00:16:10.654
(Maxley bites into the nugget)

00:16:10.654 --> 00:16:13.969
- I'm wondering now, what is the red?

00:16:13.969 --> 00:16:17.169
Hmm! That actually does taste good.

00:16:17.169 --> 00:16:20.669
(playful music continues)

00:16:22.682 --> 00:16:24.105
I don't really like it...

00:16:24.105 --> 00:16:25.384
- Oh, my God.

00:16:25.384 --> 00:16:26.865
He didn't like the sushi balls.

00:16:26.865 --> 00:16:28.355
- What are they?

00:16:28.355 --> 00:16:29.439
- Just take a bite of the middle.

00:16:29.439 --> 00:16:30.735
It's your favorite California roll!

00:16:30.735 --> 00:16:32.235
- Wait a minute...

00:16:33.084 --> 00:16:34.334
What is inside?

00:16:35.435 --> 00:16:36.602
Let's try it.

00:16:42.267 --> 00:16:46.355
It tastes like my dad's
coffee with frosting on it.

00:16:46.355 --> 00:16:47.188
(Owen stifling laughter)

00:16:47.188 --> 00:16:49.158
- Why is he drinking his
dad's coffee? (laughs)

00:16:49.158 --> 00:16:51.594
- The cake itself is okay in the middle.

00:16:51.594 --> 00:16:53.701
The colors actually
bring it a little bit up.

00:16:53.701 --> 00:16:57.467
Overall, I think the drink
is what is keeping it up.

00:16:57.467 --> 00:16:58.731
- I'm gonna lose.

00:16:58.731 --> 00:16:59.564
(cartoon flourish)

00:16:59.564 --> 00:17:01.249
- Holy smokes! I can't believe this.

00:17:01.249 --> 00:17:03.445
It kind of looks very close to it.

00:17:03.445 --> 00:17:05.086
How did they get the egg so small?

00:17:05.086 --> 00:17:06.668
- He seems stoked.

00:17:06.668 --> 00:17:09.418
- They kind of burnt it a little.

00:17:10.741 --> 00:17:12.328
It tastes lemony.

00:17:12.328 --> 00:17:13.956
It tastes okay.

00:17:13.956 --> 00:17:15.413
(Maxley chewing the sugar stick)

00:17:15.413 --> 00:17:18.545
The hard candy is really hard to bite in.

00:17:18.545 --> 00:17:20.119
That's pop rocks! (chuckles)

00:17:20.119 --> 00:17:21.751
I think we'll try the star.

00:17:21.751 --> 00:17:24.054
It's hard... or kind of.

00:17:24.054 --> 00:17:25.940
(Maxley chewing the puff star)

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:27.669
What is this?

00:17:27.669 --> 00:17:30.429
Hey, it's cool and edible.

00:17:30.429 --> 00:17:32.274
Hey, they actually do look like it.

00:17:32.274 --> 00:17:34.605
- I think I'm definitely
getting more points on accuracy.

00:17:34.605 --> 00:17:37.022
- I think I'll try this cake.

00:17:38.627 --> 00:17:40.406
Oh, I know what this is.

00:17:40.406 --> 00:17:41.398
The Loco Moco.

00:17:41.398 --> 00:17:43.050
That's actually good.

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:44.160
That is chicken.

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:45.195
The red chicken was better.

00:17:45.195 --> 00:17:46.028
(audience laughs)

00:17:46.028 --> 00:17:49.969
- He's as smart as I thought! He's good.

00:17:49.969 --> 00:17:50.802
- I knew it.

00:17:50.802 --> 00:17:51.635
It was pineapple.

00:17:51.635 --> 00:17:53.877
The green thing mixed
well with the pineapple.

00:17:53.877 --> 00:17:57.539
Overall the cake was pretty
good, and also the pineapple.

00:17:57.539 --> 00:17:59.067
Let's bring out the chefs!

00:17:59.067 --> 00:18:02.217
(playful music)

00:18:02.217 --> 00:18:03.050
- [Owen] What's up?

00:18:03.050 --> 00:18:03.883
- (chuckles) What's up?

00:18:03.883 --> 00:18:04.716
- [H] Hello, hello!

00:18:04.716 --> 00:18:05.576
- Oh, hello!

00:18:05.576 --> 00:18:06.409
- How are we doing?

00:18:06.409 --> 00:18:07.242
- Good.

00:18:07.242 --> 00:18:10.423
- All right, Maxley. Which
dish did you like more?

00:18:10.423 --> 00:18:12.173
Dish one or dish two?

00:18:14.046 --> 00:18:15.498
- Dish one.

00:18:15.498 --> 00:18:16.864
(triumphant music)

00:18:16.864 --> 00:18:17.789
(H cheers, Maxley laughs)

00:18:17.789 --> 00:18:19.043
- I won!

00:18:19.043 --> 00:18:20.046
- Here you go!

00:18:20.046 --> 00:18:21.164
- Thank you.

00:18:21.164 --> 00:18:22.039
Thank you, thank you.

00:18:22.039 --> 00:18:23.925
- Thank you for being on with me,

00:18:23.925 --> 00:18:26.678
and also baking me the
greatest lunch ever.

00:18:26.678 --> 00:18:28.229
- Aw, thank you. That was really sweet.

00:18:28.229 --> 00:18:29.934
- It's the greatest
achievement of my entire life.

00:18:29.934 --> 00:18:31.071
- Congrats, H Woo.

00:18:31.071 --> 00:18:34.137
Maxley, I hope you enjoyed your food,

00:18:34.137 --> 00:18:36.431
and I'll see you in fourth grade.

00:18:36.431 --> 00:18:38.932
Do I get a consolation prize?

00:18:38.932 --> 00:18:40.030
- Yeah, a hug.

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:41.290
- Aw, come here Maxley.

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:42.123
- Aww.

00:18:42.123 --> 00:18:42.956
Can I get a hug?

00:18:42.956 --> 00:18:43.789
- Yeah, sure.

00:18:43.789 --> 00:18:47.172
- Thank you very much
for letting me, like,

00:18:47.172 --> 00:18:48.842
eat what you made.

00:18:48.842 --> 00:18:49.675
- Thank you.

00:18:49.675 --> 00:18:50.508
- It's my honor.

00:18:50.508 --> 00:18:52.249
- It is not your honor!

00:18:52.249 --> 00:18:53.555
You get paid to do it.

00:18:53.555 --> 00:18:56.388
(everyone laughs)

00:18:57.391 --> 00:19:00.891
(playful music continues)

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:13.743
(music fades out)

